              "type": "text",
              "text": "20000 people enter a competition. There are going to be 10 winners.",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Jakub says that there is less than a 1% chance of winning the competition. Is Jakub correct?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Yes, $\\frac{10}{20\\,000}=\\frac1{2000}$, which is less than $1\\%$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{winning})&=\\frac{10}{20\\,000}\\\\P(\\text{winning})&=\\frac1{2000}\\end{align*}$$\nSince $\\frac1{2000}<\\frac1{100}=1\\%$, Jakub is correct.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 25
  },
